{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdFk5yhnwGuF175GFCey","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MmQWctyyag6WmDECE5WQ9c","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/taiga/bench/trees/taiga-3-harness; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/harness/log.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nentry='''## 2026-11-02: GitHub importer copies inline images into Taiga\n\n- **What changed.** `GithubImporter._import_inline_images` (`taiga/importers/github/importer.py`) finds the `https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/<id>` images of a description (markdown and `<img>` forms), asks GitHub to render each one to get a signed URL, downloads it, stores it as an `Attachment` of the user story or issue and rewrites the URL to `<attachment url>#_taiga-refresh=<type>:<id>`. Each distinct URL is imported once. A failed image (render, download, non-image Content-Type, save) keeps its GitHub link and logs a warning. `_import_user_stories_data` and `_import_issues_data` call it after the object is created and update the description only if it changed. Tests: `tests/integration/test_importers_github_inline_images.py`.\n- **What I learned.** `UserStoryStatus` and `IssueStatus` slugs come from the name, so factories need `name=\"open\"` to get the slug `open`. `make test` calls `make db-up`, which fails with \"port is already allocated\" when another worktree's compose Postgres already uses 5432. All worktrees then share one server and the same `test_taiga` database, so parallel `--create-db` runs can break each other. I ran the full suite with a temporary settings module that sets another `DATABASES[\"default\"][\"TEST\"][\"NAME\"]`.\n- **What is left.** Images in comments are not imported (comments go through `take_snapshot` with the raw GitHub body). Images are fetched one after the other, with two HTTP calls per image, so large imports get slower.\n\n'''\nmarker='## 2026-11-01: fast gate output shows the test run'\ns=s.replace(marker, entry+marker,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit status --short"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":800,"cache_read_input_tokens":61872,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":800},"output_tokens":33,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"baa3384c-479d-4a62-80cd-aa42e3f5ff18","uuid":"8e0031d6-7eeb-4324-ad4a-4e340bc04c86","timestamp":"2026-11-02T01:44:45.137Z","request_id":"req_011CgdFk5hqUK6ZqwvjdiWJv","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MmQWctyyag6WmDECE5WQ9c":{"command":"cd /Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/taiga/bench/trees/taiga-3-harness; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/harness/log.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nentry='''## 2026-11-02: GitHub importer copies inline images into Taiga\n\n- **What changed.** `GithubImporter._import_inline_images` (`taiga/importers/github/importer.py`) finds the `https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/<id>` images of a description (markdown and `<img>` forms), asks GitHub to render each one to get a signed URL, downloads it, stores it as an `Attachment` of the user story or issue and rewrites the URL to `<attachment url>#_taiga-refresh=<type>:<id>`. Each distinct URL is imported once. A failed image (render, download, non-image Content-Type, save) keeps its GitHub link and logs a warning. `_import_user_stories_data` and `_import_issues_data` call it after the object is created and update the description only if it changed. Tests: `tests/integration/test_importers_github_inline_images.py`.\n- **What I learned.** `UserStoryStatus` and `IssueStatus` slugs come from the name, so factories need `name=\"open\"` to get the slug `open`. `make test` calls `make db-up`, which fails with \"port is already allocated\" when another worktree's compose Postgres already uses 5432. All worktrees then share one server and the same `test_taiga` database, so parallel `--create-db` runs can break each other. I ran the full suite with a temporary settings module that sets another `DATABASES[\"default\"][\"TEST\"][\"NAME\"]`.\n- **What is left.** Images in comments are not imported (comments go through `take_snapshot` with the raw GitHub body). Images are fetched one after the other, with two HTTP calls per image, so large imports get slower.\n\n'''\nmarker='## 2026-11-01: fast gate output shows the test run'\ns=s.replace(marker, entry+marker,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit status --short"}}}
